| Connect Azure DevOps and its set-up (#3802, #3921): the **Connect Azure DevOps** sheet (Mac) and dialog (web) with two ways in. **Microsoft Entra** (#3921, dev.azure.com only): Entra's device flow (`login.microsoftonline.com/<tenant>/oauth2/v2.0/devicecode`, scope Azure DevOps's `499b84ac-…/.default offline_access`) with the Agent Loops app on Entra (#4873, `AzureDevOpsClientID`, made by `scripts/entra-app.py` in the agents' tenant) or one in the machine's secrets (`AZURE_DEVOPS_CLIENT_ID`, and `AZURE_DEVOPS_TENANT`, else `organizations`); the host checks the access token with the organization as a bearer token, keeps the pair and renews it (the row says **Microsoft Entra · renews by itself**), and the azuredevops and azureboards servers send it as Bearer. **Personal access token**: an **Organization** (dev.azure.com/acme, acme.visualstudio.com, or an Azure DevOps Server's collection) and a **Personal access token** with Code (read and write), Build (read) and Work Items (read and write), checked by the host with that organization (`GET <org>/_apis/connectionData`, Basic) and kept in its store (`connections.AzureDevOps`); its row on Your Connectors says the organization and **Personal access token**, with **Disconnect**. A folder whose remote is on dev.azure.com, `*.visualstudio.com` or the connected Azure DevOps Server (after GitHub, GitLab and Bitbucket, before Forgejo) gets Tasks (**Azure Boards work items**), Code review (**Azure Repos pull requests**) and CI (**Azure Pipelines**) from the connection, each proved by one read (the project's newest work item, the newest pull request, the newest build), and the azuredevops server's events turned on once; the azuredevops and azureboards servers and the Work pages read the connection; the connection's display name is the viewer's Azure DevOps login in the control plane's people when Settings ▸ Account gives none (#3853) | Mac, web | built, walked on scratch with a fake Azure DevOps | — | 2026-11-07, against a fake 